hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"182","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi told us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “that he wiped over ""the socks"""
"183","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb Al-Hamdani and Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, they said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka’b, on the authority of Bilal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wipe on “The socks.” Abdullah bin Saeed said, he said: Zaida told me"
"184","Abu Amr Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz told us, Muhammad bin Sawa bin Anbar Al-Sadusi told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he saw Saad bin Malik wiping over his socks, and he said: You are doing that, so we met with Umar, Saad said to Omar: Give my nephew a fatwa about wiping over the socks. Omar said: “We were with our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping over our socks, not We see harm in that.” Ibn Umar said: Even if it came from the feces? He said: “Yes.”"
